# {{FH_PROJECT}} workflow (canonical)

The single source of truth for how a {{FH_ARTIFACT_NOUN}} moves through gates.
`SKILL.md` only points here; never duplicate this content elsewhere.

## Lifecycle

1. Start a unit: `python3 harness/core/gate.py start <slug>` (owns `{{FH_UNIT_DIR}}/.active`).
2. Advance gates **in order**; each gate's command is the only way to set it.
3. A unit ends in a terminal state: the final gate, or `escalated` (with a
   written "why I'm stuck" note; never confidently ship wrong work).

